"The cache client connects lazily, disables its offline queue, permits two retries per request and gives up after five attempts with a backoff capped at two seconds. When the cache is unreachable, every read returns nothing and every write is dropped, and the application continues to serve correct results directly from the database. The same posture applies to the queue: email is sent inline when the queue is unavailable, so an invitation is never silently dropped because the backend was down; report generation falls back to inline execution for the same reason; and when the artificial-intelligence service is unavailable the curriculum-reading module still starts, replaces its upload area with an offer of manual entry, and presents the same review table for completion by hand. The intent is consistent throughout: every external service is an accelerator, and none of them is permitted to become a hard dependency of a capability the college needs.",
